What is Mockito Verification?

Mockito provides verification methods to check whether a mocked object's methods were called during test execution. It is useful for validating interactions between objects in unit testing.

Advantages
Confirms method invocation.
Checks method arguments.
Verifies the number of method calls.
Ensures methods are never called when required.
Supports flexible argument matching.
Common Verification Methods
Method	Purpose
verify()	Confirms a method was invoked.
times(n)	Checks the exact number of method calls.
never()	Verifies a method was not called.
atLeast(n)	Ensures a method was called at least n times.
anyInt()	Matches any integer argument.
anyString()	Matches any string argument.
eq()	Matches an exact argument value.
