JUnit Test Cases
1. ExternalApi Interface

The ExternalApi interface represents an external dependency used by the service.

interface ExternalApi {

    void sendData(String data);

    void processUser(int userId, String username);

    String getData();

}
Purpose
Represents an external service.
Replaced with a mock object during testing.
2. Service Class

MyService is the class being tested.

class MyService {

    private final ExternalApi externalApi;

    public MyService(ExternalApi externalApi) {
        this.externalApi = externalApi;
    }

    public void doWork() {
        externalApi.sendData("important");
    }

    public void registerUser(int id, String name) {
        externalApi.processUser(id, name);
    }

    public String fetchData() {
        return externalApi.getData();
    }
}
Purpose
Calls methods of ExternalApi.
Tested using mocked dependencies.
3. Test Cases
Test 1: Verify Method Invocation
@Test
public void testVerifySendDataCalled() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = Mockito.mock(ExternalApi.class);

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    service.doWork();

    verify(mockApi).sendData("important");

}
Explanation
Creates a mock object.
Calls doWork().
Verifies that sendData("important") was called.
Test 2: Verify Exact Arguments
@Test
public void testVerifyProcessUserWithExactArgs() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = Mockito.mock(ExternalApi.class);

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    service.registerUser(42, "Alice");

    verify(mockApi).processUser(42, "Alice");

}
Explanation
Verifies that the method received the exact arguments.
Checks both user ID and username.
Test 3: Verify Method Never Called
@Test
public void testVerifyNeverCalled() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = Mockito.mock(ExternalApi.class);

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    verify(mockApi, never()).sendData(anyString());

}
Explanation
Ensures sendData() was never executed.
Uses never() to verify zero invocations.
Test 4: Verify Number of Calls
@Test
public void testVerifyNumberOfCalls() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = Mockito.mock(ExternalApi.class);

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    service.doWork();
    service.doWork();

    verify(mockApi, times(2)).sendData("important");

}
Explanation
Calls doWork() twice.
Verifies sendData() was invoked exactly two times.
Test 5: Verify At Least Once
@Test
public void testVerifyAtLeastOnce() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = Mockito.mock(ExternalApi.class);

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    service.fetchData();
    service.fetchData();

    verify(mockApi, atLeast(1)).getData();

}
Explanation
Calls fetchData() multiple times.
Verifies getData() was called at least once.
Test 6: Verify Using Argument Matchers
@Test
public void testVerifyWithArgumentMatchers() {

    ExternalApi mockApi = Mockito.mock(ExternalApi.class);

    MyService service = new MyService(mockApi);

    service.registerUser(99, "Bob");

    verify(mockApi).processUser(anyInt(), eq("Bob"));

}
Explanation
anyInt() accepts any integer value.
eq("Bob") ensures the second argument is exactly "Bob".
Mockito Verification Flow
Create Mock Object
        │
        ▼
Inject Mock into Service
        │
        ▼
Execute Service Method
        │
        ▼
Mockito Records Calls
        │
        ▼
verify() Checks Interaction
        │
        ▼
Test Pass / Fail
Common Argument Matchers
Matcher	Description
anyInt()	Matches any integer value.
anyString()	Matches any string value.
eq(value)	Matches the specified value exactly.
any()	Matches any object.
isNull()	Matches a null value.
notNull()	Matches any non-null value.
Verification Methods Summary
Method	Description
verify(mock)	Verifies a method was called.
verify(mock, times(2))	Checks exact number of calls.
verify(mock, never())	Ensures method was never called.
verify(mock, atLeast(1))	Checks minimum number of calls.
verify(mock).method(anyInt(), eq("Bob"))	Verifies method using argument matchers.
